{"name":"Alexandria’s Lighthouse","hex":"#fcefc1","fetched":"2026-10-20","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lighthouse","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tower or other structure exhibiting a light or lights to warn or guide sailors."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lighthouse"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lighthouse","blocks":[{"text":"A lighthouse is a tower, building, or other type of physical structure designed to emit light from a system of lamps and lenses and to serve as a beacon for navigational aid for maritime pilots at sea or on inland waterways."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Aerial_photograph_60D_2012_05_13_8760_DxO_retusche.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_60D_2012_05_13_8760_DxO_retusche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lighthouse","wikidata":"Q39715"},{"title":"Alexandria","blocks":[{"text":"Alexandria is a major city in Egypt. Lying at the western edge of the Nile River Delta, it extends about 40 km (25 mi) along the country's northern coast. It is Egypt's principal seaport, the second largest city after Cairo, and the largest city on the Mediterranean coast. Founded in 331 BC by Alexander the Great, Alexandria was one of the largest and most important cities of antiquity and a leading hub for science, culture, and scholarship."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/San_Stefano_Grand_Plaza.JPG/330px-San_Stefano_Grand_Plaza.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexandria","wikidata":"Q87"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Aerial_photograph_60D_2012_05_13_8760_DxO_retusche.jpg/500px-Aerial_photograph_60D_2012_05_13_8760_DxO_retusche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Aerial_